      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-3087: shutil.unpack_archive() extracted ZIP members whose names are Windows absolute paths with a drive letter (C:\\...) outside the target directory, because only Windows treats such names as absolute. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/146581 (3.12 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/a6650a2cdf0c49fb8ce0c982903aa2aa274beefe), first released in CPython 3.12.14; see https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-3087, which states that only Windows is affected. The DHI Debian 13 python-3.12 packages are Linux builds of CPython. On Linux os.path is posixpath, where neither a drive letter nor a backslash makes a ZIP member name absolute, so zipfile extraction keeps such members inside the target directory and the vulnerable path is never reached. Builds from 3.12.14-0 also carry the upstream fix (Lib/zipfile/__init__.py and Lib/shutil.py, checked in every published build)."
    },
